Heavy metal contents in soils
Lead, Cd, Ni, Co and Cr concentrations in soil samples (Table 5) followed a
trend similar to vegetables heavy metals concentrations of vegetables. Thus, the
HEAVY METAL ACCUMULATION IN LEAFY VEGETABLES                                                47

increase of metal contents (µg g-1) in soils of medium-level and high-level
polluted areas were 109 to 274%, 104 to 173% and 112 to 269% for Pb; 126 to
187%, 162 to 164% and 119 to 157% for Cd; 132 to 185%, 169 to 189% and 102
to 171% for Ni; it was 151 to 212%, 171 to 250% and 269 to 286% for Co; and
was 142 to 174%, 151 to 178% and 154 to 159% for Cr, respectively.
Comparing the metal concentration in soil with guidelines for soils showed that
all metal concentration was below the safe limits for soils (Table 5).
